  "routing_rule": "For each single model, review its included records. For each group combination, review only records every member includes. Automatically exclude other records. Historical doubt counts as include. No automatic inclusion.",
  "human_decision_assumption": "Reviewed records receive their existing human label. Workload measures records, not screening time, reviewer errors, or disagreement resolution.",
  "interpretation": "Descriptive results on 595 labeled records. The later cohort was selected by historical unanimous inclusion. Unlabeled search results and approved removals are outside these denominators. Closed-weight LLMs retain their original inputs. Two-model unanimity is less strict than three-model unanimity. Llama uses binary constrained decoding, while Qwen and Gemma use unconstrained greedy generation with strict response validation. Observed scores do not establish performance across the entire search or a new review.",
  "metric_definitions": {
    "human_disagreements": "False inclusions plus false exclusions: FP + FN. Compare model routing decisions with human labels before human review corrects extra inclusions.",
    "inclusion_precision": "True inclusions among records sent to humans: TP / (TP + FP).",
    "exclusion_precision": "True exclusions among automatically excluded records: TN / (TN + FN). Also called negative predictive value.",
    "undefined_precision": "Undefined when no records receive that label."
  },
